NAME
       xargs - build and run command lines from standard input

SYNOPSIS
       xargs [-0rtx] [-d DELIM] [-E EOF] [-I REPL] [-L N] [-n
          N] [-s SIZE] [-P 1] [command [arg...]]

DESCRIPTION
       Reads arguments from standard input (blanks and
       newlines separate them; quotes and backslashes escape,
       except with -0 or -d) and runs the command (default
       echo) with as many as fit. Commands run one at a time:
       -P only accepts 1 (there is no parallel execution
       here). Exit status: 0, 123 a command failed, 124 a
       command exited 255, 125 a command was killed, 126
       cannot run, 127 not found, 1 other errors.

NOTES
       Runs one command at a time; -P with more than 1 prints
       a warning.

SEE ALSO
       sh(1)

